{"id": "london", "note": "Claude draft for London: dates for the undated OSM London Wall pieces and the Tower curtain wall; the full Roman-medieval London Wall circuit with its six Roman gates (demolished 1760-77), the riverside wall and the Civil War Lines of Communication; built-up area from Londinium and Lundenwic to 1900; Roman sites, Old London Bridge and other lost landmarks; Roman roads and the main later streets; the Fleet, the Walbrook, the pre-Embankment foreshore, the Roman waterfront and the filled Surrey Docks; name and date fixes. Wall and gate positions follow Merrifield and the surviving fragments (conf 2); the Lines of Communication and the 1700/1800 extents are estimates.", "features": [
